From b76e0707066af52259ae720e12fde885fceecc83 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Davide Gironi <davide.gironi@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 15:34:56 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] ASoC: ice1712: claim the second MIDI port of the PHASE 88

The PHASE 88 rack has two MIDI interfaces, one on the front panel and
one on the rear, but its EEPROM advertises a single UART, so the driver
registers one rawmidi device and the rear connector stays dead:

  $ amidi -l
  IO  hw:0,0    TerraTec Phase88 MIDI

Terratec's own driver exposes both - "[PHASE88.Interface.Midi1]" and
"[PHASE88.Interface.Midi2]" in ews88wdm.inf, "PHASE88 MIDI Port 1/2",
whose changelog line for the second one reads "17-Sep-02 (Cl) - Mic28
Extensions (Midi 2)".  Both UARTs live inside the Envy24 (MMIO
0x0c/0x0d and 0x1c/0x1d), so nothing is missing except the bit the
EEPROM should have carried; set ICE1712_CFG_2xMPU401 in the same place
the board's other EEPROM errors are corrected.

Verified on a PHASE 88 rack: with a loopback cable in the rear connector
a SysEx frame written to the second UART came back on it byte-exactly
(three frames, no byte differences), and the first UART - the front
connector, which worked before - still works.  With both ports
registered and idle the card raised no interrupt on its IRQ line for
10 s, so an unconnected input does not put traffic on the shared
interrupt line.
---
 sound/pci/ice1712/ice1712.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 19 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/pci/ice1712/ice1712.c b/sound/pci/ice1712/ice1712.c
index 18e4f43a4..528c4938f 100644
--- a/sound/pci/ice1712/ice1712.c
+++ b/sound/pci/ice1712/ice1712.c
@@ -2312,6 +2312,25 @@ static int snd_ice1712_chip_init(struct snd_ice1712 *ice)
 		 * codec behind them.
 		 */
 		ice->eeprom.data[ICE_EEP1_CODEC] |= ICE1712_CFG_NO_CON_AC97;
+		/*
+		 * The rack has two MIDI interfaces - one on the front panel, one
+		 * on the rear - but the EEPROM advertises only one UART, so
+		 * without this the rear connector stays dead.  Terratec's own
+		 * driver exposes both: "[PHASE88.Interface.Midi1]" and
+		 * "[PHASE88.Interface.Midi2]" in ews88wdm.inf, "PHASE88 MIDI Port
+		 * 1/2", the changelog naming the second one "Mic28 Extensions
+		 * (Midi 2)".  Both UARTs are inside the Envy24, so claiming the
+		 * second one is only a matter of setting the bit the EEPROM
+		 * should have carried.
+		 *
+		 * Verified on a PHASE 88 rack: with a loopback cable in the rear
+		 * connector, a SysEx frame written to the second UART came back
+		 * on it byte-exactly, and the first UART (front connector) kept
+		 * working as before.  With the second UART enabled and both ports
+		 * idle the card raised no interrupt on its IRQ line for 10 s,
+		 * so an unconnected input does not generate traffic.
+		 */
+		ice->eeprom.data[ICE_EEP1_CODEC] |= ICE1712_CFG_2xMPU401;
 	}
 	pci_write_config_byte(ice->pci, 0x60, ice->eeprom.data[ICE_EEP1_CODEC]);
 	pci_write_config_byte(ice->pci, 0x61, ice->eeprom.data[ICE_EEP1_ACLINK]);
